# Five closures meet at the parameter of `run`, so its call is a call of the lost functions, and `wrap` is one of them: it is entered with one argument, `true`. If a function that only passes its rest list on heard of the calls that name it alone, the second parameter of `take` would be proven a string while `run(wrap)` leaves it `undefined`, and the first an `i32` while it is `true`.
#   function take(a, b) { return b; }  function wrap(...list) { return take(...list); }  function run(f) { return f(true); }  wrap(1, "x"); run(wrap); run(other4); run(other5); run(other6); run(other7);
